    "durationMs": 253437,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation** (module `benchmark.local/app`, chi v5.2.1 kept as-is):\n- `cmd/server/main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment, applies migrations, serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` (`PORT` overridable)\n- `internal/store/` — persistence via `database/sql` + pgx v5 (`lib/pq`'s modern replacement): create/get/increment/list, plus an embedded-SQL migration runner that tracks applied versions in a `schema_migrations` table so reruns only apply pending ones\n- `internal/api/api.go` — chi routes: `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` with `422`/`409`/`404` JSON error bodies\n- `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — `links` table with unique code, click counter, identity id for creation ordering\n- `start.sh` — rebuilds the binary if a Go toolchain is present (falls back to the prebuilt `bin/server`), then serves in the foreground; migrations run inside the server before listening\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verification** (all via the real Postgres at `postgres:5432`):\n- Full curl battery: auto/custom code creation, URL echoed unchanged with query/fragment, duplicate → 409, every invalid-URL and invalid-code shape (bad scheme, no host, too short/long codes, unicode, malformed JSON) → 422 with `error` field, boundary 4-char and 20-char codes accepted, unknown codes → 404, redirect → 302 with correct `Location`\n- Clicks: exactly +1 per redirect, exactly +50 under 50 concurrent redirects (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`)\n- Persistence: killed and restarted the server — data and click counts survived\n- Cold start: deleted `bin/`, ran `sh start.sh` — rebuilt, migrated, served; dependencies were installed during development so nothing is fetched at startup"
  }
